WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:01.530
- [Voice Over] Today on Couch Tomatoes,

00:00:01.530 --> 00:00:03.360
we're talking all things Emmys.

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:04.193
- I'll tell you one thing,

00:00:04.193 --> 00:00:05.850
if we lose it certainly won't be for

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:08.410
lack of touching people in a Denny's.

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:09.840
Hello everybody!

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:10.820
- What's up everyone?

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:11.653
I'm Naz Perez

00:00:11.653 --> 00:00:14.040
and welcome to the brand-new
show from Rotten Tomatoes,

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:15.020
Couch Tomatoes.

00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:17.010
Brought to you by Freschetta.

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:17.843
Here's the thing,

00:00:17.843 --> 00:00:19.920
with TV and all these
new streaming services,

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:21.930
it's so hard to choose what to watch on TV

00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:23.970
because there's so many
good options out there.

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:25.550
Which is why here on Couch Tomatoes

00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:26.580
we're gonna help you guys out.

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:28.440
And we're actually kicking
off our first episode

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:29.670
talking all things Emmys,

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:31.350
because the Emmys are this Sunday.

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:33.290
And lucky for me, I'm
not doing this alone.

00:00:33.290 --> 00:00:34.690
Joining me on the couch today is

00:00:34.690 --> 00:00:35.900
senior editor at TV Guide,

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:36.794
Malcolm Venable.

00:00:36.794 --> 00:00:37.627
- Hey.

00:00:37.627 --> 00:00:39.950
- Fandango's Film and TV
correspondent Nikki Novak.

00:00:39.950 --> 00:00:42.170
And IndieWire's Ben Travers.

00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:43.003
Hello guys!

00:00:43.003 --> 00:00:43.836
- [Nikki] Hi.
- [Malcolm] Hello.

00:00:43.836 --> 00:00:46.740
- I feel I have the Golden
State Warriors of the Emmys.

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:48.210
(guests laugh) You know what I mean?

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:50.150
You guys watch so much television.

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:51.769
I can't wait to hear your predictions.

00:00:51.769 --> 00:00:53.410
Before we get into predictions though,

00:00:53.410 --> 00:00:54.930
I really want to talk
about the big stories

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:56.990
that everyone's talking
about when it comes to Emmys.

00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:58.960
Starting with 'Game of Thrones,' right?

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:01.830
I mean, a whopping 32 Emmy nominations.

00:01:01.830 --> 00:01:03.890
They already stole 10 of
them this past weekend

00:01:03.890 --> 00:01:05.460
at the Creative Arts Emmys.

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:08.030
However, they had a
controversial last season, right?

00:01:08.030 --> 00:01:10.140
58% on the Tomatometer.

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:12.920
Think the series average
is 89% on the Tomatometer.

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:15.020
A lot of people feel like
the final season was rushed.

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:17.340
We saw caramel macchiatos on set.

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:20.360
So Ben, I want to start off with you.

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:21.700
Do you feel like this final season

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:24.010
is gonna taint 'Games of Thrones'' legacy?

00:01:24.010 --> 00:01:25.080
Or do you feel like

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:27.810
the Emmy voters are actually
gonna honor 'Game of Thrones'?

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:28.670
- I think it's both.

00:01:28.670 --> 00:01:31.190
I think the final season
kinda tainted its own legacy,

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:32.410
but in terms of The Emmys,

00:01:32.410 --> 00:01:34.323
they're gonna give it
all the awards still.

00:01:34.323 --> 00:01:35.942
They're so locked in at this point

00:01:35.942 --> 00:01:37.620
because there's just not a lot

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:39.160
of strong competition out there.

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:40.300
Like, the other shows are great,

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:41.640
but they're not as beloved.

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:43.330
They're not as instilled
within the academy

00:01:43.330 --> 00:01:44.163
as 'Game of Thrones.'

00:01:44.163 --> 00:01:46.180
So they're still gonna
make a run on Sunday

00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:48.130
and it's gonna be a lot of wins.

00:01:48.130 --> 00:01:50.000
- There's a lot of shows that also

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:51.280
wouldn't qualify this season.

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:52.200
Like 'Westworld.'

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:53.500
We didn't see 'Handmaid's Tale.'

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:54.370
A lot of shows,

00:01:54.370 --> 00:01:55.203
and 'The Crown,'

00:01:55.203 --> 00:01:56.850
that we would normally
see go up against them,

00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:58.330
and I think that's part of the reason

00:01:58.330 --> 00:01:59.917
we saw more nominations.

00:01:59.917 --> 00:02:02.070
- Yeah, there's still
nothing like it on television

00:02:02.070 --> 00:02:05.970
in terms of scope and scale
and production and story.

00:02:05.970 --> 00:02:07.280
- Do you guys feel like Emmy voters

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:08.937
tend to favor final seasons?

00:02:08.937 --> 00:02:10.270
- I think they do

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:13.010
when it's the right
kind of timing, I guess.

00:02:13.010 --> 00:02:15.200
You've seen it happen with
stuff like 'Breaking Bad.'

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:16.858
They got really, really
excited for those final,

00:02:16.858 --> 00:02:20.620
that final season, slash two
split seasons of 'Breaking Bad'

00:02:20.620 --> 00:02:21.610
and they really wanted to give it

00:02:21.610 --> 00:02:22.930
as many awards as they possibly could,

00:02:22.930 --> 00:02:24.940
despite a lot of intense
competition out there.

00:02:24.940 --> 00:02:27.250
But 'Mad Men''s final
season was widely ignored.

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:28.860
John Hamm was able to pull off a win

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:29.727
because he just hadn't done it yet.

00:02:29.727 --> 00:02:31.110
- [Naz] Right.
- [Ben] But they felt like

00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:32.660
they'd honored it so many times already

00:02:32.660 --> 00:02:34.240
that they were kinda done with it.

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:36.210
- I feel like now that it's
been a couple of months

00:02:36.210 --> 00:02:37.160
since the last episode

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:39.570
and people's madness has
sort of cooled off a bit.

00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:41.700
It's the writers that
people are mad at primarily.

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:43.150
Not necessarily the actors

00:02:43.150 --> 00:02:44.640
and I think that's where you're gonna see,

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:45.710
I'm even hearing words,

00:02:45.710 --> 00:02:47.027
like the word sweep.

00:02:47.027 --> 00:02:48.040
This week.

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:49.760
That there could be a
sweep of 'Game of Thrones.'

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:51.860
So I think that people are
sort of getting behind it again

00:02:51.860 --> 00:02:53.040
and want to see,

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:54.990
it was a cultural phenomenon.

00:02:54.990 --> 00:02:56.620
You're not gonna see anything
like it for a long time,

00:02:56.620 --> 00:02:57.453
if ever.

00:02:57.453 --> 00:02:58.286
- Thank heaven.

00:02:58.286 --> 00:03:00.090
(everyone laughs)

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:00.923
- Are you tired of it?

00:03:00.923 --> 00:03:02.840
- I'm not a Throner.

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:03.834
I mean, it's fine.

00:03:03.834 --> 00:03:05.720
I'm like, who are all these people?

00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:07.170
I don't know all their names.

00:03:08.906 --> 00:03:09.739
- He admits it!

00:03:09.739 --> 00:03:11.120
I love that you're admitting this!

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:12.770
- Yeah, this is better
than watching football.

00:03:12.770 --> 00:03:13.960
I'm like, I don't know
who these people are

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:14.880
under the helmets.

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:16.450
But what's interesting
about the final season

00:03:16.450 --> 00:03:17.283
of 'Game of Thrones,'

00:03:17.283 --> 00:03:18.480
and you were mentioning madness,

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:20.450
is that when HBO was
getting a lot of flak

00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:21.548
for this final season,

00:03:21.548 --> 00:03:23.690
'Chernobyl' kinda came up out of nowhere

00:03:23.690 --> 00:03:26.010
and was this instant success for HBO.

00:03:26.010 --> 00:03:26.843
And it got me thinking

00:03:26.843 --> 00:03:28.370
about the next big story at Emmys

00:03:28.370 --> 00:03:29.370
that everyone's talking about

00:03:29.370 --> 00:03:31.268
which is lead actor in a limited series,

00:03:31.268 --> 00:03:34.490
where Jared Harris from
'Chernobyl' is actually nominated.

00:03:34.490 --> 00:03:35.970
When I look at this category,

00:03:35.970 --> 00:03:37.280
it's really insane you guys.

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:38.810
You have all these Oscar winners,

00:03:38.810 --> 00:03:41.360
Benicio Del Toro, Mahershala
Ali, Sam Rockwell.

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:43.440
All up for their first Emmy ever.

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:45.480
But really the buzz is around

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:47.750
Jharrel Jerome and Jared Harris.

00:03:47.750 --> 00:03:49.870
So, Malcolm, I wanna hear from you first.

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:51.090
Do these two stand a chance

00:03:51.090 --> 00:03:53.040
against these seasoned actors?

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:53.900
- Absolutely.

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:55.460
But I think it's gonna go to Jharrel.

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:58.553
I mean, he's just 21, which is remarkable.

00:04:00.373 --> 00:04:02.550
He did such a phenomenal
job in 'When They See Us.'

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:05.630
But I think there's specific things

00:04:05.630 --> 00:04:07.500
that work in his favor
from that performance.

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:08.490
The story is timely.

00:04:08.490 --> 00:04:10.740
It's about social justice.

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:12.330
He was the only person in the cast

00:04:12.330 --> 00:04:16.060
to play a younger version
of the same person.

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:16.893
- [Naz] Right.

00:04:16.893 --> 00:04:19.090
- And then he had a
entire episode to himself,

00:04:19.090 --> 00:04:20.420
where he was in solitary confinement,

00:04:20.420 --> 00:04:21.294
and he just really kind of

00:04:21.294 --> 00:04:22.570
broke out of the confines

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:24.850
of what you even expect
to see on television.

00:04:24.850 --> 00:04:25.840
It was just fantastic.

00:04:25.840 --> 00:04:27.255
If he doesn't win, I'm rioting.

00:04:27.255 --> 00:04:28.088
I'm fighting.

00:04:28.088 --> 00:04:29.410
I'm putting that out there.

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:30.243
- I'm putting it out there

00:04:30.243 --> 00:04:31.952
that someone with the
letter J is gonna win

00:04:31.952 --> 00:04:33.500
(everyone laughs) this category.

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:34.800
No, I think it's between the two.

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:36.100
And I think even though we have legends,

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:37.140
I think it's

00:04:37.140 --> 00:04:38.770
social relevance and buzz.

00:04:38.770 --> 00:04:41.140
And 'Chernobyl' and When
'They See Us' have that.

00:04:41.140 --> 00:04:42.840
So between the two, I keep going,

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:44.570
this is one of my toughest categories.

00:04:44.570 --> 00:04:45.403
When we get to the predictions

00:04:45.403 --> 00:04:46.620
I still don't know what I'm gonna say.

00:04:46.620 --> 00:04:48.950
It's gonna be either Jared or Jharrel.

00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:49.783
- Yeah.

00:04:49.783 --> 00:04:50.850
In terms of the Oscar winners out there

00:04:50.850 --> 00:04:52.250
I really think Mahershala Ali

00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:55.010
is the leader of that squadron of folk.

00:04:55.010 --> 00:04:55.930
I think he delivered

00:04:55.930 --> 00:04:57.954
such an incredible
performance on 'True Detective.'

00:04:57.954 --> 00:04:59.180
But at the same time,

00:04:59.180 --> 00:05:00.013
I feel like,

00:05:00.013 --> 00:05:02.090
we've given it to Mahershala before.

00:05:02.090 --> 00:05:03.730
He's won two Oscars now.

00:05:03.730 --> 00:05:05.455
He's very well-known, very respected.

00:05:05.455 --> 00:05:07.154
I think it's probably time

00:05:07.154 --> 00:05:08.870
to share the wealth a little bit.

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:10.280
And I think people are really excited,

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:12.120
especially given how many nominations,

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:13.782
when they see who else is
in the acting categories,

00:05:13.782 --> 00:05:15.007
to award someone from that cast,

00:05:15.007 --> 00:05:16.600
and Jharrel's the man.

00:05:16.600 --> 00:05:18.120
- Yeah, and I think a couple years ago,

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:21.110
if a film actor did a TV show,

00:05:21.110 --> 00:05:22.570
we kinda assumed they
were gonna win the Emmy,

00:05:22.570 --> 00:05:24.650
and I don't think we're
necessarily seeing that anymore.

00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:25.770
- Right, which is crazy.

00:05:25.770 --> 00:05:27.530
But you brought up something
that got me thinking.

00:05:27.530 --> 00:05:29.150
Between Jharrel and Jared,

00:05:29.150 --> 00:05:30.970
because I'm also torn between these two.

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:32.320
There's this kind of

00:05:32.320 --> 00:05:34.179
generational struggle here.

00:05:34.179 --> 00:05:37.001
Do you award someone who's
been at it for a while,

00:05:37.001 --> 00:05:38.790
who gave us a stand-out performance?

00:05:38.790 --> 00:05:39.932
Or do you award the person

00:05:39.932 --> 00:05:41.540
with his breakthrough performance

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:43.610
so early on in his acting career?

00:05:43.610 --> 00:05:44.443
- I still say Jharrel.

00:05:44.443 --> 00:05:46.240
It gives the Emmys an opportunity

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:48.010
to be, for lack of a better word,

00:05:48.010 --> 00:05:48.843
hipper and cooler.

00:05:48.843 --> 00:05:51.000
Because Jharrel's a kid.
- Got it.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:52.043
- He's not even 22 yet.

00:05:52.043 --> 00:05:53.889
- But Jared Harris, I will argue,

00:05:53.889 --> 00:05:55.870
he is sort of an unsung hero.

00:05:55.870 --> 00:05:57.650
He has been around for so long

00:05:57.650 --> 00:05:59.220
and hasn't necessarily got the accolades

00:05:59.220 --> 00:06:01.440
as some of the bigger
stars in this category.

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:02.670
- He was nominated for 'Mad Man'

00:06:02.670 --> 00:06:03.990
and a lot of people were actually upset

00:06:03.990 --> 00:06:05.950
that he wasn't nominated for first season

00:06:05.950 --> 00:06:07.610
of AMC's 'The Terror,' so.

00:06:07.610 --> 00:06:08.443
- Yeah.

00:06:08.443 --> 00:06:09.530
So I think it would be one of those things

00:06:09.530 --> 00:06:10.980
where if he did win,

00:06:10.980 --> 00:06:11.990
I don't think

00:06:11.990 --> 00:06:13.740
anybody would be necessarily mad at that

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:15.270
because he does have that body of work.

00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:16.620
And hasn't been a name,

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:18.480
he's been in so many things

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:20.280
and he's that person
that's just not a big star.

00:06:20.280 --> 00:06:21.640
But he's deserving.

00:06:21.640 --> 00:06:22.810
- And weirdly enough, it feels like,

00:06:22.810 --> 00:06:23.643
you mentioned,

00:06:23.643 --> 00:06:24.700
he's broken out on TV already.

00:06:24.700 --> 00:06:26.650
And he's had enough roles through 'Mad Men,'

00:06:26.650 --> 00:06:28.030
through 'The Terror,' through 'The Crown,'

00:06:28.030 --> 00:06:29.870
where it's like he should
have been recognized

00:06:29.870 --> 00:06:31.468
more than he has been with the Emmys,

00:06:31.468 --> 00:06:32.590
which makes me think

00:06:32.590 --> 00:06:34.763
that they're just not
as big a fans perhaps

00:06:34.763 --> 00:06:36.160
as the rest of the world.

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:38.260
Or at least the rest of the TV community.

00:06:38.260 --> 00:06:40.060
- Well one person they're not slow for is

00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:41.770
Miss Julia Louis-Dreyfus.

00:06:41.770 --> 00:06:43.920
I mean, next to the word
Emmy winner in the dictionary

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:45.080
I feel is her face.

00:06:45.080 --> 00:06:46.315
But before we get to Julia,

00:06:46.315 --> 00:06:48.570
Nikki and I actually sat down earlier

00:06:48.570 --> 00:06:50.210
to talk about all the must-haves you need

00:06:50.210 --> 00:06:52.450
for an awards-worthy watch party.

00:06:52.450 --> 00:06:53.720
Check it out.

00:06:53.720 --> 00:06:54.553
All right guys,

00:06:54.553 --> 00:06:56.420
so aside from hooking you
up with all our predictions,

00:06:56.420 --> 00:06:58.170
we're also gonna tell you how to spice up

00:06:58.170 --> 00:07:00.120
your award show watch party this weekend.

00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:02.110
- I'm actually having one at my place.

00:07:02.110 --> 00:07:03.330
I need a little help with this.

00:07:03.330 --> 00:07:04.890
What do you think that I should serve?

00:07:04.890 --> 00:07:06.480
- OK, so whenever I have a party

00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:07.700
I always serve pizza

00:07:07.700 --> 00:07:09.070
because you can't go wrong with pizza.

00:07:09.070 --> 00:07:10.140
It makes the party.

00:07:10.140 --> 00:07:11.140
- If somebody doesn't like pizza,

00:07:11.140 --> 00:07:11.973
I don't like them.

00:07:11.973 --> 00:07:13.110
- [Naz] Yeah! No, I agree.

00:07:13.110 --> 00:07:14.060
And when I throw a party,

00:07:14.060 --> 00:07:15.380
my go-to is Freschetta.

00:07:15.380 --> 00:07:17.270
Because they have so
many different flavors.

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:18.370
They're just made better.

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:21.090
And this rising crust
pepperoni is always a hit.

00:07:21.090 --> 00:07:21.923
- It looks amazing.

00:07:21.923 --> 00:07:23.030
- Yeah, people are obsessed with it.

00:07:23.030 --> 00:07:23.863
- I'm set for that.

00:07:23.863 --> 00:07:24.790
So now I'm thinking pairings.

00:07:24.790 --> 00:07:26.960
I know red wine always
goes well with pizza,

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:27.793
but what do you think?

00:07:27.793 --> 00:07:29.580
Champagne, cocktails?

00:07:29.580 --> 00:07:30.840
- I think it's fun to switch it up.

00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:33.210
I think people forget
that pizza goes so well

00:07:33.210 --> 00:07:35.030
with so many different drink pairings.

00:07:35.030 --> 00:07:36.900
My personal favorite pizza with champagne

00:07:36.900 --> 00:07:39.670
is actually this brick
oven spinach and mushroom.

00:07:39.670 --> 00:07:40.503
- Diving in.

00:07:40.503 --> 00:07:42.600
- There's something about the
earthiness of the mushroom

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:44.590
that just goes so well with the rich,

00:07:44.590 --> 00:07:45.860
fruitiness of the Champagne.

00:07:45.860 --> 00:07:46.980
When I'm throwing a party

00:07:46.980 --> 00:07:48.970
I always like to elevate the experience

00:07:48.970 --> 00:07:51.410
and I throw a little gin, lemon, and sugar

00:07:51.410 --> 00:07:52.243
in the Champagne.

00:07:52.243 --> 00:07:53.230
It's called a French 75.

00:07:53.230 --> 00:07:54.630
And that is also always a hit.

00:07:54.630 --> 00:07:55.920
- You are so fancy.

00:07:55.920 --> 00:07:56.753
You really need

00:07:56.753 --> 00:07:57.620
to come to my party.
- I try.

00:07:57.620 --> 00:07:59.240
- You're invited.
- Oh my God, thanks!

00:07:59.240 --> 00:08:01.010
If you're serving Freschetta
and Champagne, I'm there.

00:08:01.010 --> 00:08:02.240
- Yay! Cheers.

00:08:02.240 --> 00:08:03.090
- Cheers.

00:08:03.090 --> 00:08:04.840
Okay, let's talk about
Julia Louis-Dreyfus.

00:08:04.840 --> 00:08:06.730
I feel like she has more
gold statues in her house

00:08:06.730 --> 00:08:08.020
than the city of Dubai.

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:09.560
She could soon hold

00:08:09.560 --> 00:08:12.020
the most Emmys for a
performer of all time.

00:08:12.020 --> 00:08:14.940
She's currently tied with
Cloris Leachman for eight.

00:08:14.940 --> 00:08:17.090
Nikki, does anyone stand a chance

00:08:17.090 --> 00:08:19.830
against Julia in the lead
actress for a comedy series?

00:08:19.830 --> 00:08:20.761
- I think this is the biggest lock

00:08:20.761 --> 00:08:22.610
of everything at the Emmys.

00:08:22.610 --> 00:08:23.810
But it's so much of a lock,

00:08:23.810 --> 00:08:26.070
that it's reminding me of
Glenn Close at the Oscars.

00:08:26.070 --> 00:08:27.407
How everybody thought she was gonna win,

00:08:27.407 --> 00:08:29.480
but then there was a shock
when Olivia Colman won.

00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:31.760
So that's the only thing I think.

00:08:31.760 --> 00:08:34.070
Barring a shocking moment like that,

00:08:34.070 --> 00:08:35.010
I think she's a lock.

00:08:35.010 --> 00:08:37.398
I think she's been a superstar
through this whole thing.

00:08:37.398 --> 00:08:39.539
I think if they're gonna award the show

00:08:39.539 --> 00:08:41.110
for their last season,

00:08:41.110 --> 00:08:42.760
it might not necessarily go to 'Veep,'

00:08:42.760 --> 00:08:44.809
but Julia will be the
person that's gonna win.

00:08:44.809 --> 00:08:45.796
- Yeah, and I mean

00:08:45.796 --> 00:08:47.310
I think over the last few years

00:08:47.310 --> 00:08:50.100
when 'Veep' was a sure thing
in a lot of categories,

00:08:50.100 --> 00:08:52.457
that it felt even more like Julia was,

00:08:52.457 --> 00:08:53.977
she was gonna take it.

00:08:53.977 --> 00:08:55.140
You just wrote that off.

00:08:55.140 --> 00:08:55.987
You didn't worry about it.

00:08:55.987 --> 00:08:57.970
But because it's a little
bit weaker this year

00:08:57.970 --> 00:09:00.400
because other comedies
have more nominations

00:09:00.400 --> 00:09:02.299
than HBO's crown jewel,

00:09:02.299 --> 00:09:03.960
maybe this is the year

00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:05.360
where Julia finally slips off.

00:09:05.360 --> 00:09:07.500
Maybe this is the time
when Phoebe Waller-Bridge

00:09:07.500 --> 00:09:08.680
sneaks in for 'Fleabag.'

00:09:08.680 --> 00:09:10.850
Or Natasha Lyonne sneaks
in for 'Russian Doll.'

00:09:10.850 --> 00:09:12.800
Both of those got some
Creative Arts Emmy love

00:09:12.800 --> 00:09:13.750
this past weekend,

00:09:13.750 --> 00:09:14.654
which was really exciting.

00:09:14.654 --> 00:09:16.470
You know, it could happen.

00:09:16.470 --> 00:09:17.303
I'm still with you,

00:09:17.303 --> 00:09:18.360
I still think Julia's got it,

00:09:18.360 --> 00:09:20.014
but I'm a little more nervous than normal.

00:09:20.014 --> 00:09:22.700
- Well you know, I say
when it comes to the Emmys

00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:24.404
it's like Jan Brady's,

00:09:24.404 --> 00:09:26.073
"Julia, Julia, Julia."

00:09:26.073 --> 00:09:26.906
It's hers.

00:09:26.906 --> 00:09:27.739
It's hers.

00:09:27.739 --> 00:09:29.670
Does Miss Brosnahan have a chance her?

00:09:29.670 --> 00:09:32.980
She did one last year when
Julia wasn't eligible.

00:09:32.980 --> 00:09:34.830
- If it was a should win category

00:09:34.830 --> 00:09:36.320
I would choose Rachel.

00:09:36.320 --> 00:09:38.960
Because I think she continues
to excel on that show.

00:09:38.960 --> 00:09:40.527
But I think that show will clean up

00:09:40.527 --> 00:09:41.707
but I don't necessarily,

00:09:41.707 --> 00:09:42.600
what?

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:43.433
- [Ben] Sorry.

00:09:43.433 --> 00:09:45.540
I can't get on board with this nonsense.

00:09:45.540 --> 00:09:46.373
This is,

00:09:46.373 --> 00:09:48.700
this is a lot.
- Nonsense?

00:09:48.700 --> 00:09:50.122
Over Phoebe?

00:09:50.122 --> 00:09:53.230
- I would put Rachel like
fourth or fifth billed

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:54.881
on just charge of deserving winner.

00:09:54.881 --> 00:09:55.714
- Yeah, this go round.

00:09:55.714 --> 00:09:57.040
It's Julia and then Phoebe.

00:09:57.040 --> 00:09:59.268
- In terms of what you feel or would.

00:09:59.268 --> 00:10:00.101
- It's Phoebe and then Julia.

00:10:00.101 --> 00:10:01.760
- Well then we can't leave
out Catherine O'Hara too,

00:10:01.760 --> 00:10:02.593
because--

00:10:02.593 --> 00:10:03.426
- Well, Catherine O'Hara.

00:10:03.426 --> 00:10:04.967
- [Nikki] Moira Rose.
I mean,

00:10:04.967 --> 00:10:06.840
- [Nikki] How is no one even
talking about Catherine?

00:10:06.840 --> 00:10:08.320
- [Malcolm] And this will be her second

00:10:08.320 --> 00:10:09.189
since like 1980,

00:10:09.189 --> 00:10:11.630
she hasn't won since 1982
or something like that.

00:10:11.630 --> 00:10:13.308
And she's such a beloved character.

00:10:13.308 --> 00:10:15.180
Not that the other ones aren't,

00:10:15.180 --> 00:10:16.020
but I mean.

00:10:16.020 --> 00:10:16.990
- But is this a viable--

00:10:16.990 --> 00:10:17.823
- Moira Rose is iconic.

00:10:17.823 --> 00:10:20.370
- Is an iconic TV character.

00:10:20.370 --> 00:10:21.470
I'm shocked that more people

00:10:21.470 --> 00:10:22.303
aren't talking about.

00:10:22.303 --> 00:10:23.210
- I think people are though.

00:10:23.210 --> 00:10:24.470
I think in terms of an upset,

00:10:24.470 --> 00:10:25.970
that name is getting bounced around

00:10:25.970 --> 00:10:26.803
as much as Phoebe's name is.

00:10:26.803 --> 00:10:28.710
And I think that's another person

00:10:28.710 --> 00:10:29.543
that if she were to win,

00:10:29.543 --> 00:10:30.570
people would jump to their feet.

00:10:30.570 --> 00:10:31.403
- Absolutely.

00:10:31.403 --> 00:10:32.500
- It would just be a huge moment.

00:10:32.500 --> 00:10:33.760
- Although Julia might hit her,

00:10:33.760 --> 00:10:35.119
beat her in the parking lot or something.

00:10:35.119 --> 00:10:35.952
(everyone laughs)

00:10:35.952 --> 00:10:38.780
- As Selina or as herself? (laughs)

00:10:38.780 --> 00:10:39.830
- I wanna take a second

00:10:39.830 --> 00:10:41.840
and talk about first time nominees

00:10:41.840 --> 00:10:43.910
and some fresh faces.

00:10:43.910 --> 00:10:45.210
Who are some first time nominees

00:10:45.210 --> 00:10:47.760
that you think people should
be paying attention to?

00:10:47.760 --> 00:10:49.680
- I'm team Jharrel Jerome.

00:10:49.680 --> 00:10:52.000
Again, we know him from his

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:53.800
outstanding turn in 'Moonlight.'

00:10:53.800 --> 00:10:55.920
Which seems like ancient history

00:10:55.920 --> 00:10:58.023
when it was only a couple
of years ago. (laughs)

00:10:58.023 --> 00:11:00.530
And to think he's this
young kid from the Bronx

00:11:00.530 --> 00:11:01.720
who actually never even thought

00:11:01.720 --> 00:11:04.330
that he'd be able to become an actor.

00:11:04.330 --> 00:11:06.110
I mean, so many boxes get checked here.

00:11:06.110 --> 00:11:09.990
He's fantastic for
representation of Latin and

00:11:09.990 --> 00:11:11.680
African American performances.

00:11:11.680 --> 00:11:13.760
This story is timely relevant.

00:11:13.760 --> 00:11:15.450
Socially conscious.

00:11:15.450 --> 00:11:16.970
The material that he had to work with

00:11:16.970 --> 00:11:18.420
is obviously outstanding.

00:11:18.420 --> 00:11:19.253
- Nikki?

00:11:19.253 --> 00:11:20.086
- I concur.

00:11:20.086 --> 00:11:21.098
But I'm gonna throw
in an Anthony Carrigan.

00:11:21.098 --> 00:11:23.124
I absolutely

00:11:23.124 --> 00:11:25.140
love him on 'Barry.'

00:11:25.140 --> 00:11:26.940
It is one of my favorite shows.

00:11:26.940 --> 00:11:28.580
But that character, NoHo Hank,

00:11:28.580 --> 00:11:29.450
he's such a standout.

00:11:29.450 --> 00:11:30.660
Every time he comes on screen,

00:11:30.660 --> 00:11:31.980
as much as I love the other actors,

00:11:31.980 --> 00:11:33.573
he steals every scene he's in.

00:11:33.573 --> 00:11:36.870
And I think he's pretty much a long-shot

00:11:36.870 --> 00:11:37.703
in terms of a win,

00:11:37.703 --> 00:11:38.900
but I'm so glad he was nominated.

00:11:38.900 --> 00:11:41.374
- And he's making no eyebrows

00:11:41.374 --> 00:11:43.087
look fabulous. (everyone laughs)

00:11:43.087 --> 00:11:44.060
- Yes!

00:11:44.060 --> 00:11:44.893
That's hard to do,

00:11:44.893 --> 00:11:45.950
because I've had that before.

00:11:45.950 --> 00:11:46.783
- It's hard to do.
- And trust me,

00:11:46.783 --> 00:11:48.520
the alien look is not good.

00:11:48.520 --> 00:11:49.860
- I'm waiting for thin
eyebrows to come back,

00:11:49.860 --> 00:11:51.410
so I can be in again.

00:11:51.410 --> 00:11:53.700
- And mine is Jodie Comer for 'Killing Eve.'

00:11:53.700 --> 00:11:56.340
Who I just feel like is on fire right now.

00:11:56.340 --> 00:11:58.170
We're just kinda waiting
with baited breath

00:11:58.170 --> 00:12:00.120
to see what else she's gonna get to do.

00:12:00.120 --> 00:12:02.390
Because she's so good on 'Killing Eve.'

00:12:02.390 --> 00:12:04.630
And creating an assassin in 2019

00:12:04.630 --> 00:12:05.900
who's unique and stands out

00:12:05.900 --> 00:12:07.060
and that people wanna keep watching

00:12:07.060 --> 00:12:08.320
and are interested in

00:12:08.320 --> 00:12:12.340
and doesn't just fit the
mold of previous characters,

00:12:12.340 --> 00:12:14.050
she's done that and then so much more.

00:12:14.050 --> 00:12:15.030
- I'm just throwing out there,

00:12:15.030 --> 00:12:16.900
she should be a Marvel superhero.

00:12:16.900 --> 00:12:19.258
I think she would make a great--

00:12:19.258 --> 00:12:20.091
- That is such a great--

00:12:20.091 --> 00:12:20.924
- She's new, she's fresh.

00:12:20.924 --> 00:12:21.840
She's a great actress.

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:23.040
And she has a presence.

00:12:23.040 --> 00:12:24.690
- As far as fresh faces for me,

00:12:24.690 --> 00:12:26.478
I'm really into Joey King right now.

00:12:26.478 --> 00:12:28.250
What she did in 'The Act,'

00:12:28.250 --> 00:12:30.860
the physical transformation
to shaving her head,

00:12:30.860 --> 00:12:32.790
I feel like she gave us such a deep

00:12:32.790 --> 00:12:33.940
and mature performance

00:12:33.940 --> 00:12:34.910
and we're so used to seeing her

00:12:34.910 --> 00:12:36.770
in these kid and teen-friendly movies

00:12:36.770 --> 00:12:38.460
like 'The Kissing Booth' on Netflix.

00:12:38.460 --> 00:12:41.000
And just the video that she
uploaded on social media

00:12:41.000 --> 00:12:41.833
when she got nominated,

00:12:41.833 --> 00:12:42.870
it actually made me cry.

00:12:42.870 --> 00:12:45.030
I'm really excited for
her that she's nominated,

00:12:45.030 --> 00:12:46.520
and I just can't wait to
see what she does next.

00:12:46.520 --> 00:12:48.050
- She reminds me of a Natalie Portman.

00:12:48.050 --> 00:12:49.990
Like how she was a young
actress that you just knew

00:12:49.990 --> 00:12:51.870
was gonna be a massive
actress when she got older.

00:12:51.870 --> 00:12:52.840
She's that person.

00:12:52.840 --> 00:12:53.673
Yeah.

00:12:53.673 --> 00:12:54.506
- OK guys,

00:12:54.506 --> 00:12:56.040
so I feel we got through
all the big stories.

00:12:56.040 --> 00:12:57.750
We got through all the first time nominees

00:12:57.750 --> 00:12:59.380
that we think you guys
should watch out for.

00:12:59.380 --> 00:13:01.690
But now I want to go
through each major category

00:13:01.690 --> 00:13:02.790
and know who your predictions are.

00:13:02.790 --> 00:13:04.440
Because I have a car payment to pay off

00:13:04.440 --> 00:13:05.765
and I'm gonna be making
some bets this weekend.

00:13:05.765 --> 00:13:06.620
(Malcolm chuckles)

00:13:06.620 --> 00:13:08.970
So I wanna hear who
you guys predict to win

00:13:08.970 --> 00:13:10.210
and then after you guys tell me

00:13:10.210 --> 00:13:11.230
I'm actually gonna tell you guys

00:13:11.230 --> 00:13:12.920
what the RT staff pick is.

00:13:12.920 --> 00:13:14.520
And so these are the expect predictions

00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:16.300
for the nominees on TV's biggest night,

00:13:16.300 --> 00:13:17.800
based on the combined ballots

00:13:17.800 --> 00:13:20.420
of the editorial team
here at Rotten Tomatoes.

00:13:20.420 --> 00:13:22.090
So, first one

00:13:22.090 --> 00:13:23.640
Lead Actress in a Comedy Series.

00:13:23.640 --> 00:13:24.840
We obviously talked about this

00:13:24.840 --> 00:13:25.760
when we talked about Julia.

00:13:25.760 --> 00:13:26.957
But I wanna know down the line,

00:13:26.957 --> 00:13:28.938
who do you guys think is
gonna win this weekend?

00:13:28.938 --> 00:13:29.771
- Julia.

00:13:29.771 --> 00:13:30.760
- Julia.

00:13:30.760 --> 00:13:31.593
- Julia.

00:13:31.593 --> 00:13:32.700
- Julia, Julia, Julia!

00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:33.533
- And Julia!

00:13:33.533 --> 00:13:35.445
- She's like Tom Brady
at a Super Bowl right now!

00:13:35.445 --> 00:13:36.278
(everyone laughs)

00:13:36.278 --> 00:13:38.060
She's just a shoe-in.

00:13:38.060 --> 00:13:39.430
And surprise, surprise guys,

00:13:39.430 --> 00:13:42.610
the RT staff pick is
also Julia Louis-Dreyfus,

00:13:42.610 --> 00:13:45.210
so I will be shocked if she
doesn't win this Sunday.

00:13:45.210 --> 00:13:46.043
- I think she will too.

00:13:46.043 --> 00:13:48.160
(everyone laughs)

00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:50.410
- Okay, so Lead Actor in a Comedy Series.

00:13:50.410 --> 00:13:51.630
When I look at this category

00:13:51.630 --> 00:13:53.880
I think there's a lot of showbiz
legends in this category.

00:13:53.880 --> 00:13:54.823
You've got Ted Danson,

00:13:54.823 --> 00:13:56.130
Michael Douglas,

00:13:56.130 --> 00:13:57.000
Eugene Levy.

00:13:57.000 --> 00:13:58.061
And then you have Bill Hader,

00:13:58.061 --> 00:13:59.860
who's nominated again.

00:13:59.860 --> 00:14:01.640
Won this category last year.

00:14:01.640 --> 00:14:03.113
So who do you guys predict to win?

00:14:03.113 --> 00:14:04.241
- Bill, again.

00:14:04.241 --> 00:14:05.074
- Bill, again.

00:14:05.074 --> 00:14:05.907
- Bill, again.

00:14:05.907 --> 00:14:06.740
- Bill Hader's gonna win this.

00:14:06.740 --> 00:14:07.580
He's the IT guy.

00:14:07.580 --> 00:14:08.413
The IT movie.

00:14:08.413 --> 00:14:10.590
And he is the IT guy of the season.

00:14:10.590 --> 00:14:13.120
- Yeah, they're not done
rewarding Bill Hader just yet.

00:14:13.120 --> 00:14:14.140
He's gonna win.

00:14:14.140 --> 00:14:14.973
- OK.

00:14:14.973 --> 00:14:17.750
Well the RT staff pick also
thinks it's Bill Hader.

00:14:17.750 --> 00:14:19.800
So, hopefully he takes that.

00:14:19.800 --> 00:14:22.590
Okay, so Outstanding Comedy Series.

00:14:22.590 --> 00:14:24.210
And I wanna make note that no show

00:14:24.210 --> 00:14:25.760
that's won for its first season

00:14:25.760 --> 00:14:27.565
has ever won for its final season.

00:14:27.565 --> 00:14:28.810
'cause I feel like a lot of people

00:14:28.810 --> 00:14:29.820
are looking at 'Veep,' right?

00:14:29.820 --> 00:14:30.830
'cause it's the final season.

00:14:30.830 --> 00:14:32.120
So who do you guys predict to win

00:14:32.120 --> 00:14:33.620
Outstanding Comedy on Sunday?

00:14:33.620 --> 00:14:35.390
- So, I think 'Veep' is gonna win,

00:14:35.390 --> 00:14:37.150
although I'd like 'Fleabag' to win,

00:14:37.150 --> 00:14:38.066
'Veep' will win.

00:14:38.066 --> 00:14:38.899
- All right.

00:14:38.899 --> 00:14:39.732
- I disagree.

00:14:39.732 --> 00:14:40.565
I don't think it's gonna be Veep.

00:14:40.565 --> 00:14:42.230
I think 'Veep' only has, I
think eight total nominations?

00:14:42.230 --> 00:14:44.250
I think 'The Marvelous Mrs. Maisel'

00:14:44.250 --> 00:14:45.660
is flying under the radar,

00:14:45.660 --> 00:14:47.067
just because we kinda go,

00:14:47.067 --> 00:14:48.610
"OK, we've heard it, we've heard it."

00:14:48.610 --> 00:14:51.410
But I really think that 20
nominations are impressive.

00:14:51.410 --> 00:14:53.590
But I think 'Marvelous
Mrs. Maisel' is gonna win.

00:14:53.590 --> 00:14:55.450
- I was actually team 'Barry'

00:14:55.450 --> 00:14:57.440
up until the Creative Arts Awards,

00:14:57.440 --> 00:15:00.370
and then after 'Maisel' just
kinda dominated that scene

00:15:00.370 --> 00:15:01.650
in a way that we didn't expect,

00:15:01.650 --> 00:15:03.800
I'm starting to come onto the 'Maisel' side,

00:15:03.800 --> 00:15:04.633
and officially I'm gonna go 'Maisel.'

00:15:04.633 --> 00:15:05.560
- Did I just win you over?

00:15:05.560 --> 00:15:06.393
- Yeah.

00:15:06.393 --> 00:15:07.226
(everyone laughs)

00:15:07.226 --> 00:15:09.530
- The RT staff pick, guys, is 'Fleabag.'

00:15:09.530 --> 00:15:11.500
And I also think 'Fleabag' is gonna take it.

00:15:11.500 --> 00:15:13.270
I think 'Fleabag' is gonna do an upset.

00:15:13.270 --> 00:15:14.103
- Thank you for validating me.

00:15:14.103 --> 00:15:16.250
(everyone laughs)

00:15:16.250 --> 00:15:17.350
- OK, let's move on to

00:15:17.350 --> 00:15:19.760
Lead Actress in a Limited Series.

00:15:19.760 --> 00:15:21.610
This category is very interesting, right?

00:15:21.610 --> 00:15:24.610
Patricia Arquette won the
Globe for 'Escape at Dannemora,'

00:15:24.610 --> 00:15:26.840
but this time Michelle
Williams is in the mix.

00:15:26.840 --> 00:15:28.410
Who do you guys have winning

00:15:28.410 --> 00:15:29.904
Lead Actress in a Limited Series?

00:15:29.904 --> 00:15:31.224
- I say Michelle Williams.

00:15:31.224 --> 00:15:32.057
It has to.

00:15:32.057 --> 00:15:33.890
It's just a phenomenal performance,

00:15:33.890 --> 00:15:34.730
and on top of that,

00:15:34.730 --> 00:15:36.000
I think

00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:38.720
the story that is running tangent

00:15:38.720 --> 00:15:40.400
to the actual show has been great.

00:15:40.400 --> 00:15:42.010
So I think Michelle
Williams is the winner.

00:15:42.010 --> 00:15:43.410
- Nikki?
- I have nothing more to add,

00:15:43.410 --> 00:15:44.950
so I concur about Michelle Williams,

00:15:44.950 --> 00:15:46.710
but I need to give a
shout out to Amy Adams.

00:15:46.710 --> 00:15:47.543
She will not win,

00:15:47.543 --> 00:15:49.241
but she was so outstanding
in 'Sharp Objects'

00:15:49.241 --> 00:15:50.220
- It's gonna be Michelle.

00:15:50.220 --> 00:15:52.060
She's got so much love around town.

00:15:52.060 --> 00:15:54.310
Like, the response that
people have shown her

00:15:54.310 --> 00:15:55.940
for during the FYC screenings,

00:15:55.940 --> 00:15:58.080
during her campaigning around town.

00:15:58.080 --> 00:15:59.160
It's been overwhelming,

00:15:59.160 --> 00:16:00.380
and I think she's gonna take it.

00:16:00.380 --> 00:16:01.850
- I think she's so deserving of it too.

00:16:01.850 --> 00:16:03.940
And the RT staff pick agrees.

00:16:03.940 --> 00:16:06.060
Michelle Williams for 'Fosse/Verdon.'

00:16:06.060 --> 00:16:08.690
OK, Lead Actor in a Limited Series.

00:16:08.690 --> 00:16:10.890
We kinda talked about this
at the top of the show.

00:16:10.890 --> 00:16:12.940
We didn't really talk
about Hugh Grant too much.

00:16:12.940 --> 00:16:14.620
It was there for 'A Very English Scandal,'

00:16:14.620 --> 00:16:15.800
and then kind of just went away.

00:16:15.800 --> 00:16:18.449
Who do you guys predict to
win this category this Sunday?

00:16:18.449 --> 00:16:19.282
- Jharrel.

00:16:19.282 --> 00:16:20.115
- Jharrel Jerome.

00:16:20.115 --> 00:16:21.510
- This is the toughest one for me.

00:16:21.510 --> 00:16:22.960
But I'm going with Jharrel.

00:16:22.960 --> 00:16:24.297
- I'm going with Jharrel as well.

00:16:24.297 --> 00:16:27.420
I feel like he's captured
the momentum at this point,

00:16:27.420 --> 00:16:29.780
and also they love that show.

00:16:29.780 --> 00:16:31.940
- It would be so epic to see him win, too.

00:16:31.940 --> 00:16:34.790
Over all these seasoned
actors in the category.

00:16:34.790 --> 00:16:36.540
But the RT staff pick actually thinks

00:16:36.540 --> 00:16:38.178
it's gonna go to Jared
Harris for 'Chernobyl.'

00:16:38.178 --> 00:16:39.011
- [Malcolm] Ooh.

00:16:39.011 --> 00:16:40.440
- Which I would also be
happy to see him take that.

00:16:40.440 --> 00:16:42.600
Okay, let's talk about
Outstanding Limited Series.

00:16:42.600 --> 00:16:45.000
We kinda talked about this
at the top of the show.

00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:46.010
When I look at this category,

00:16:46.010 --> 00:16:47.858
all of these shows are
based on real life events,

00:16:47.858 --> 00:16:49.800
except for 'Sharp Objects.'

00:16:49.800 --> 00:16:51.860
And I feel like the race
here is really between

00:16:51.860 --> 00:16:54.050
'Chernobyl' and 'When They See Us.'

00:16:54.050 --> 00:16:57.460
Both powerful stories that
portray these great injustices

00:16:57.460 --> 00:16:59.060
that came out of woeful ignorance.

00:16:59.060 --> 00:17:01.080
Who do you guys predict
to win this Sunday?

00:17:01.080 --> 00:17:02.383
- I say 'When They See Us.'

00:17:03.460 --> 00:17:05.600
You know, we've talked about
the social injustice aspect

00:17:05.600 --> 00:17:07.113
but it's also really well done.

00:17:07.113 --> 00:17:08.690
- This was the trickiest one for me.

00:17:08.690 --> 00:17:09.740
It was so, so tough.

00:17:09.740 --> 00:17:10.690
It's so neck and neck.

00:17:10.690 --> 00:17:12.520
And I really had 'When They See Us,'

00:17:12.520 --> 00:17:13.900
but with the Creative Arts Emmys,

00:17:13.900 --> 00:17:16.540
'Chernobyl' just upped
the anti a little bit.

00:17:16.540 --> 00:17:18.160
I think it has the slight edge right now.

00:17:18.160 --> 00:17:19.410
But it could go either way.

00:17:19.410 --> 00:17:20.420
I'd be happy with either,

00:17:20.420 --> 00:17:21.643
but I think it's gonna be 'Chernobyl.'

00:17:21.643 --> 00:17:22.832
- I actually agree with you

00:17:22.832 --> 00:17:24.720
in the sense that I think
'Chernobyl' has the edge right now,

00:17:24.720 --> 00:17:26.270
but I'm sticking with 'When They See Us.'

00:17:26.270 --> 00:17:28.910
- So Nikki, the RT staff pick
actually agrees with you.

00:17:28.910 --> 00:17:30.130
And they're going with 'Chernobyl.'

00:17:30.130 --> 00:17:32.730
So this will be a really fun
category to watch on Sunday.

00:17:32.730 --> 00:17:35.520
OK, moving on to Lead
Actress in a Drama Series.

00:17:35.520 --> 00:17:38.200
This category has a
staggering seven nominees.

00:17:38.200 --> 00:17:40.740
Ben, you kinda talked about
this at the top of the show.

00:17:40.740 --> 00:17:43.854
I feel like the race here is
between Sandra Oh and Jodie.

00:17:43.854 --> 00:17:45.370
For the same show.

00:17:45.370 --> 00:17:46.980
So who do you guys predict?

00:17:46.980 --> 00:17:48.170
- Sandra.

00:17:48.170 --> 00:17:49.003
- Sandra Oh.

00:17:49.003 --> 00:17:51.440
- I like Jodie better this season,

00:17:51.440 --> 00:17:53.240
but she didn't win before.

00:17:53.240 --> 00:17:55.690
And this is a historic moment for her.

00:17:55.690 --> 00:17:57.159
And for

00:17:57.159 --> 00:17:58.770
women of Asian descent as well.

00:17:58.770 --> 00:18:01.530
Not that that's the thing that's
gonna carry her necessarily

00:18:01.530 --> 00:18:03.870
but she still did a phenomenal job

00:18:03.870 --> 00:18:05.490
so I'm going with Sandra.

00:18:05.490 --> 00:18:07.370
- I'm actually gonna go outside
of the box a little bit.

00:18:07.370 --> 00:18:08.750
I'm gonna go with Emilia Clark.

00:18:08.750 --> 00:18:10.770
I think it's gonna be a surprise
there for 'Game of Thrones.'

00:18:10.770 --> 00:18:12.590
I think she's so beloved.

00:18:12.590 --> 00:18:16.320
I think she's been nominated
before, several times.

00:18:16.320 --> 00:18:17.370
And I think,

00:18:17.370 --> 00:18:19.990
this is the last chance
for her to get this win.

00:18:19.990 --> 00:18:21.170
So I think it's gonna be her.

00:18:21.170 --> 00:18:22.003
- If that's the win,

00:18:22.003 --> 00:18:23.240
then that's the one I'll riot for.

00:18:23.240 --> 00:18:25.085
So while you're rioting for Jharrel,

00:18:25.085 --> 00:18:26.900
I'll be very angry if Emilia wins,

00:18:26.900 --> 00:18:28.400
especially because Sandra and Jodie

00:18:28.400 --> 00:18:30.605
are just so good in 'Killing Eve.'

00:18:30.605 --> 00:18:31.730
Yeah, I think it's Sandra.

00:18:31.730 --> 00:18:33.270
- Oh, well it's interesting

00:18:33.270 --> 00:18:35.440
because the RT staff pick
also think it's Sandra.

00:18:35.440 --> 00:18:37.060
But Sandra has also never won an Emmy.

00:18:37.060 --> 00:18:38.670
- Yeah!
- It's crazy!

00:18:38.670 --> 00:18:42.140
Okay, let's move onto Lead
Actor in a Drama Series.

00:18:42.140 --> 00:18:43.630
This category is really interesting

00:18:43.630 --> 00:18:46.730
because Billy Porter is
the only first time nominee

00:18:46.730 --> 00:18:49.200
yet I'm hearing a lot of buzz about him.

00:18:49.200 --> 00:18:50.390
What do you guys predict?

00:18:50.390 --> 00:18:51.890
- Yeah, it's Billy Porter.

00:18:51.890 --> 00:18:52.723
And he deserves it.

00:18:52.723 --> 00:18:54.880
And I think it's been so great to see

00:18:54.880 --> 00:18:56.800
his campaigning for it.

00:18:56.800 --> 00:18:59.540
And the ways he talks about
having been overlooked

00:18:59.540 --> 00:19:01.570
as a performer for most of his career.

00:19:01.570 --> 00:19:03.810
And now to be in a position
where he's the lead.

00:19:03.810 --> 00:19:05.550
I think people love it.

00:19:05.550 --> 00:19:07.660
And have great feelings
about the show and him.

00:19:07.660 --> 00:19:09.360
So I'd say Billy's the winner.

00:19:09.360 --> 00:19:10.260
- What do you think?
- I agree.

00:19:10.260 --> 00:19:11.160
I think it's Billy's.

00:19:11.160 --> 00:19:13.520
I think Billy is by far the frontrunner

00:19:13.520 --> 00:19:15.060
in this category.

00:19:15.060 --> 00:19:17.290
- I think it's a little
bit closer than that.

00:19:17.290 --> 00:19:19.328
I do think that Jason
Bateman has a shot for 'Ozark,'

00:19:19.328 --> 00:19:20.960
but I am gonna go with Billy Porter.

00:19:20.960 --> 00:19:23.248
I think 'Pose' has that slight edge.

00:19:23.248 --> 00:19:25.040
- And guys, surprise surprise,

00:19:25.040 --> 00:19:28.050
the RT staff pick is also
for Billy Porter for 'Pose.'

00:19:28.050 --> 00:19:30.710
So I really hope we see
him win this this Sunday.

00:19:30.710 --> 00:19:34.052
Moving onto the big one,
Outstanding Drama Series.

00:19:34.052 --> 00:19:36.069
Do we still think it's gonna be 'GOT'?

00:19:36.069 --> 00:19:37.311
- Yeah.
- Yeah?

00:19:37.311 --> 00:19:39.380
- It's definitely 'Game of Thrones.'

00:19:39.380 --> 00:19:40.460
- If you want to get your new car...

00:19:40.460 --> 00:19:41.755
(everyone laughs)

00:19:41.755 --> 00:19:43.254
- Put it on 'Game of Thrones'?

00:19:43.254 --> 00:19:44.087
- That's gonna be the one, yeah.

00:19:44.087 --> 00:19:45.300
- Yeah, again, your odds
are gonna be terrible.

00:19:45.300 --> 00:19:47.560
But I would bet the
car on 'Game of Thrones.'

00:19:47.560 --> 00:19:48.980
I think if there's an upset lurking,

00:19:48.980 --> 00:19:49.950
which there isn't,

00:19:49.950 --> 00:19:51.450
it would be 'Succession.'

00:19:51.450 --> 00:19:53.370
If only because it's gained so much buzz

00:19:53.370 --> 00:19:54.360
for its second season.

00:19:54.360 --> 00:19:56.540
And people have really picked
up on it a little bit late.

00:19:56.540 --> 00:19:58.750
And maybe enough people like it

00:19:58.750 --> 00:20:00.020
and HBO wants to see it.

00:20:00.020 --> 00:20:00.853
But it's not gonna happen.

00:20:00.853 --> 00:20:01.910
It's still gonna be 'Game of Thrones.'

00:20:01.910 --> 00:20:04.640
- Okay, and the RT staff pick also agrees

00:20:04.640 --> 00:20:05.900
that it's gonna be 'Game of Thrones.'

00:20:05.900 --> 00:20:08.440
So guys, thank you so much
for all your predictions.

00:20:08.440 --> 00:20:10.810
Hopefully we got all of you
guys back at home set up

00:20:10.810 --> 00:20:12.800
so you're ready to go on Sunday.

00:20:12.800 --> 00:20:13.633
But before we go,

00:20:13.633 --> 00:20:14.466
I wanna talk to you guys

00:20:14.466 --> 00:20:16.020
about what your fresh picks are.

00:20:16.020 --> 00:20:18.550
So these are shows that
are nominated for an Emmy,

00:20:18.550 --> 00:20:20.400
but maybe are a little
bit under the radar.

00:20:20.400 --> 00:20:21.680
So what show do you think everyone

00:20:21.680 --> 00:20:22.930
should add to their watch list?

00:20:22.930 --> 00:20:24.117
- I'd say 'Twilight Zone.'

00:20:24.117 --> 00:20:27.410
Kumail Nanjiani is nominated
for his performance

00:20:27.410 --> 00:20:29.687
in the first episode of the new

00:20:29.687 --> 00:20:32.410
CBS All Access take on the series.

00:20:32.410 --> 00:20:34.282
And he plays this stand up comedian

00:20:34.282 --> 00:20:37.204
who's in this warped, demented universe

00:20:37.204 --> 00:20:40.350
where he has the ability
to make people die

00:20:40.350 --> 00:20:42.260
with his routine.

00:20:42.260 --> 00:20:43.560
And I thought it was fantastic.

00:20:43.560 --> 00:20:44.868
- I want to have that ability.

00:20:44.868 --> 00:20:46.101
(everyone laughs)

00:20:46.101 --> 00:20:48.011
- Is that not what we're doing right now?

00:20:48.011 --> 00:20:48.844
I thought we were deciding the Emmys

00:20:48.844 --> 00:20:51.447
as we said no to some and yes to others.

00:20:51.447 --> 00:20:53.110
- My pick, you just mentioned.

00:20:53.110 --> 00:20:53.943
'Succession.'

00:20:53.943 --> 00:20:55.676
A minute into it, I
was hooked on the show.

00:20:55.676 --> 00:21:00.370
But, if people for whatever
reason, haven't stuck with it

00:21:00.370 --> 00:21:02.763
episode five is when it really kicks in.

00:21:03.894 --> 00:21:05.050
And it goes to another level.

00:21:05.050 --> 00:21:05.883
Do you agree with me

00:21:05.883 --> 00:21:06.716
on that one?
- Yeah I do.

00:21:06.716 --> 00:21:07.640
- It goes to another level.

00:21:07.640 --> 00:21:09.443
And also, season two.

00:21:09.443 --> 00:21:11.110
The most highly addictive show.

00:21:11.110 --> 00:21:12.300
If you want to get less sleep,

00:21:12.300 --> 00:21:13.133
watch that show.

00:21:13.133 --> 00:21:13.966
(everyone laughs)

00:21:13.966 --> 00:21:14.799
- What a recommendation.

00:21:14.799 --> 00:21:15.774
Sleep less.

00:21:15.774 --> 00:21:19.655
But no, my fresh pick is
actually 'Big Mouth' on Netflix.

00:21:19.655 --> 00:21:21.760
A new season is just around the corner.

00:21:21.760 --> 00:21:23.710
It was nominated for
Best Animated Program.

00:21:23.710 --> 00:21:25.550
It's co-created by Nick Kroll

00:21:25.550 --> 00:21:26.880
as well as a slew of other people.

00:21:26.880 --> 00:21:28.150
It's got a great voice cast.

00:21:28.150 --> 00:21:31.240
Maya Rudolph absolutely
owns the whole thing.

00:21:31.240 --> 00:21:33.680
She pops up in just the most amazing ways

00:21:33.680 --> 00:21:35.475
and the way she says bubble
bath, you'll never forget.

00:21:35.475 --> 00:21:36.308
(everyone laughs)

00:21:36.308 --> 00:21:38.223
- I'm going with 'Fosse/Verdon.'

00:21:38.223 --> 00:21:40.290
Because I love Broadway, you guys,

00:21:40.290 --> 00:21:42.370
but I never knew the
behind the scenes stories

00:21:42.370 --> 00:21:44.020
of Bob Fosse and Gwen Verdon.

00:21:44.020 --> 00:21:45.070
We talked about Michelle Williams,

00:21:45.070 --> 00:21:47.270
she is so unreal in this.

00:21:47.270 --> 00:21:48.687
I was watching the
episodes and I was like,

00:21:48.687 --> 00:21:50.067
"Can someone get a Tony Award

00:21:50.067 --> 00:21:52.920
"for a theatrical performance on screen?"

00:21:52.920 --> 00:21:54.240
Asking for Michelle Williams.

00:21:54.240 --> 00:21:55.520
It is just so good.

00:21:55.520 --> 00:21:58.070
FX series produced by Lin-Manuel Miranda,

00:21:58.070 --> 00:22:00.090
and I feel like a lot of
people didn't watch it.

00:22:00.090 --> 00:22:01.263
I think it came out right before

00:22:01.263 --> 00:22:03.023
season eight of 'Game of Thrones.'

00:22:03.023 --> 00:22:04.920
So I feel like it got lost in the shuffle

00:22:04.920 --> 00:22:06.380
with all the amazing limited series,

00:22:06.380 --> 00:22:08.330
but I just love, love, love 'Fosse/Verdon.'

00:22:08.330 --> 00:22:09.730
All right guys, well that's our show.

00:22:09.730 --> 00:22:11.060
That's all the time we have for today.

00:22:11.060 --> 00:22:12.420
I wanna thank you guys so much.

00:22:12.420 --> 00:22:13.970
I feel like we covered so much ground

00:22:13.970 --> 00:22:15.000
when it comes to Emmys.

00:22:15.000 --> 00:22:17.810
If you guys wanna see a
full list of predictions

00:22:17.810 --> 00:22:18.643
from Rotten Tomatoes,

00:22:18.643 --> 00:22:19.998
head over to rottentomatoes.com.

00:22:19.998 --> 00:22:22.030
Also let us know in the comments section,

00:22:22.030 --> 00:22:23.870
what your thoughts and
what your predictions are.

00:22:23.870 --> 00:22:25.620
If you agree or disagree with us.

00:22:25.620 --> 00:22:27.280
We really wanna hear from you guys.

00:22:27.280 --> 00:22:28.113
And don't forget

00:22:28.113 --> 00:22:29.880
to hit that subscribe button
and notification bell.

00:22:29.880 --> 00:22:32.570
It is free, and you won't
miss any future episode

00:22:32.570 --> 00:22:33.403
of Couch Tomatoes.

00:22:33.403 --> 00:22:35.560
Thank you so much for tuning
into the first episode.

00:22:35.560 --> 00:22:38.360
The first one we're doing is
'American Horror Story 1984.'

00:22:38.360 --> 00:22:39.815
I am so excited.

00:22:39.815 --> 00:22:41.820
Thank you to Malcolm, Nikki, and Ben

00:22:41.820 --> 00:22:43.055
for joining me today guys.

00:22:43.055 --> 00:22:43.910
- Great.
- Woo!

00:22:43.910 --> 00:22:46.020
- I'm Naz Prez, and we'll
see you guys next time.

00:22:46.020 --> 00:22:46.853
- Cheers.
- Hey.

00:22:46.853 --> 00:22:48.626
- To Julia!
- To Julia! (laughs)

00:22:48.626 --> 00:22:51.209
(upbeat music)

